        <div class="col-md-12 col-lg-11 text-center" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="300" data-aos-duration="500">
          <p>We strongly believe by focusing on social, emotional, and ethical learning we can address a myriad of challenges and situations that individuals encounter in various aspects of life. In academic settings, students often face bullying, peer pressure, and stress, which can negatively impact their emotional well-being. By emphasizing social and emotional learning, schools can create a supportive environment where students develop resilience, self-awareness, and interpersonal skills, effectively navigating these challenges.</p>
          <p>Moreover, ethical learning helps individuals grapple with moral dilemmas and make principled decisions, preparing them for ethical challenges in their personal and professional lives. In the workplace, emphasizing these aspects contributes to the creation of a positive organizational culture, fostering teamwork, communication, and ethical conduct.</p>

