            <h2 class="text-white">Interventions</h2>
          </div>
          <p>To bring SEEL to life across the education system, a series of interconnected interventions have been designed—focusing on policy alignment, capacity building, and creating emotionally enriching school environments.</p>
          <ul class="list">
            <li>A state strategy for SEE Learning is co-created to integrate SEEL into the state curriculum framework.</li>
            <li>SEEL-based assessments are introduced to make student evaluations more holistic and emotionally informed.</li>
            <li>A cadre of SEEL Ambassadors is developed to support officials and nurture a SEEL-enabled ecosystem.</li>
            <li>SEEL Ambassadors play a key role in spreading awareness and implementing SEEL principles at various levels.</li>
            <li>Middle managers are empowered to lead SEEL implementation in schools and sustain the initiative over time.</li>
            <li>The impact of SEEL is demonstrated through school-level interventions in grades 6–12.</li>
            <li>Creative initiatives like “Khushiyon ki Deewar” (Walls of Happiness) and SEEL Corners are established to foster positive, inclusive learning spaces.</li>
            <li>The overarching goal is to systematically embed SEEL into the education system, promoting emotional well-being and ethical learning.</li>
          </ul>
